While playing nethack, recently, I came upon a level with a dwarf who
had a pick-axe.  As I expected, by the time my character met up
with said dwarf, the dwarf had chipped away at a good chunk of two rooms
leaving lots of rocks and boulders.  Now, if my character digs (I have my
own pick-axe, legacy of another dwarf from a previous level), I never get
any boulders (just rocks, and *only* if I chip away at a big boulder).

So, is the dwarf "making" the boulders or are they just generated by
the program?  If the dwarf *is* making the boulders, why doesn't my
character ever make boulders after digging?

--

Also, while playing the same game, on another level, I dug my way into
a vault, and low and behold, a vault guard was already there!
(He said something like "So that's how it is, Rogue!" or something
like that).  I immediately ran (knowing I would probably get *killed*),
and sure enough did (with a single hit from the guard).  So why was the
guard already in the vault-room?

[My only reasoning is that, maybe, this was a ghost level from a bones
file, where I had gotten killed after teleporting into the vault, and
trying to (re)pick up the gold after dropping, and the ghost of my
former self was inside the vault!].

Charlie

